		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","text":"### Uncertainty<br><br>- Abstract-only sources keep their limit<br>- Effect sizes are population averages<br>- Reviews inherit the biases of their studies","x":-1977,"y":4265,"width":500,"height":330,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","text":"### Open questions<br><br>- What design would let a claim about a mechanism be tested rather than merely observed?<br>- Which confounders can be measured, and which only randomised assignment can balance?<br>- How far can a result travel before the population no longer matches?","x":-1937,"y":4645,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"6"},
